    "result_text": "All 11 test classes (Cp01\u2013Cp11, 21 tests) pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe request asked: when `sharesHousehold` is true, allow an owner at an address already used by a same-lastName owner, assign both the same stable `householdId`, and return it. The skip-the-409 half already existed (`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`); I added the `householdId` assignment and exposure.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `householdId` field mapped to a new `household_id` column, with getter/setter.\n\n2. **DB schemas** \u2014 added `household_id VARCHAR(64)` to the `owners` table in all four schemas (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests, plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n3. **OpenAPI** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `readOnly` `householdId` property to the `Owner` response schema. This flows through to the generated `OwnerDto` and is mapped automatically by MapStruct (by name), so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns it.\n\n4. **New pipeline step** `AssignHousehold.java`, wired into `owners.POST.yml` after `build`. When the request opts in via `sharesHousehold` **and** an existing owner matches the same normalized last name + address (same normalization rule the existing uniqueness check uses):\n   - reuses an existing member's `householdId` if one exists, otherwise derives a stable `HH-<12 hex>` id from the household's normalized last name + address (deterministic, so the same household always yields the same value);\n   - assigns it to the new owner **and** back-fills any matching existing member that lacks one, saving them \u2014 so \"both\" carry the same id.\n   - Does nothing when the request doesn't opt in or there's no matching owner (a lone owner has no household to share), leaving `householdId` absent.\n\nThe `Cp11` test confirms two joiners at an existing owner's address share a non-blank `householdId`; `Cp10`'s existing behavior (409 without opt-in, allowed with it) is preserved.",
